From 948d36feeba006dadbc51a936e00603158227e76 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Simone Rota <simone.rota16@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 23:53:49 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 17/18] test: add the benchmarks of the FLC 2026/27 project

Eight self-checking applications (AES-128, binary search tree, expression
compiler and VM, FFT, Huffman coding, LU solver, PID controller, Sobel filter)
and fourteen microbenchmarks, each stressing one feature of C: annotations,
callbacks into libc, constructors and thread-local storage, dynamic memory,
floating-point special values, globals reached through pointers, integer
corner cases, a goto-based lexer, recursion, setjmp/longjmp, structs passed by
value, unions and bit-fields, variadic functions, VLAs and alloca.

They are deterministic, print a summary of their results and report the
detections of ASPIS on stderr. All the 55 combinations of data protection and
control-flow checking pass with the fixes of this series (1210/1210).
